flowchart TD
    accTitle: Web Scraper collection, saved-data and History architecture
    accDescr: An explicit POST passes Express validation and a run service before dispatching one of four bounded source adapters. Validated records or a failure outcome are persisted in MongoDB. Saved-data GET requests read the repository without dispatching a collector. Separate explicit PATCH and confirmed DELETE requests pass History validation and guarded repository mutations to archive, restore or remove stored payloads. Running runs are protected and deleted identities are retained to prevent replay. History actions never dispatch a collector.
    UI[React workspace] -->|Explicit POST| API[Express validation]
    API --> Run[Run service]
    Run -->|Save running attempt| DB[(MongoDB)]
    Run -->|Dispatch after admission| Adapter[Bounded source adapter]
    Adapter --> Amazon[Amazon: ZenRows Fetch and Cheerio]
    Adapter --> Indeed[Indeed: ZenRows Fetch and Python BeautifulSoup]
    Adapter --> Booking[Booking: ZenRows Browser, Playwright and BeautifulSoup]
    Adapter --> Tiobe[TIOBE: public HTTP and Cheerio]
    Amazon --> Result[Validate normalized records or classify failure]
    Indeed --> Result
    Booking --> Result
    Tiobe --> Result
    Result -->|Persist terminal outcome| DB
    UI -->|Saved-data GET| Read[Run repository reads]
    Read --> DB
    DB -->|Saved records and metadata| Read
    Read -->|Validated response| UI
    UI -->|Explicit PATCH or confirmed DELETE| Manage[Express and run service: validate History action]
    Manage --> Mutation[Run repository: guarded History mutation]
    Mutation -->|Archive, restore or delete| DB
